Input: {"question": "Who is the creator of \"I Will Follow\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d00", "start": 0, "end": 56, "text": "I Will Follow \"I Will Follow\" is a song by rock band U2."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d00", "start": 57, "end": 178, "text": "It is the opening track from their debut album, \"Boy\", and it was released as the album's second single, in October 1980."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d00", "start": 179, "end": 291, "text": "Lead singer Bono wrote the lyrics to \"I Will Follow\" in tribute to his mother who died when he was 14 years old."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d00", "start": 292, "end": 400, "text": "\"I Will Follow\" is the only song that U2 have performed on every tour since they released their first album."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d00", "start": 401, "end": 481, "text": "The song was U2's first music video, directed by Meiert Avis in Dublin, Ireland."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d00", "start": 482, "end": 522, "text": "The song was issued five times, first in"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d01", "start": 0, "end": 412, "text": "] 6.1 1981 release [ edit ] 6.2 1982 release [ edit ] 6.3 1983 release [ edit ] Contents [ ] [ hide ] 1 Composition and releases 2 Live performances 3 Reception and legacy 4 Track listings 5 Chart positions 5.1 1981 release 5.2 1982 release 5.3 1983 release 6 See also 7 References 8 External links Composition and releases [ edit ] [ ] `` I Will Follow '' was written three weeks before U2 began recording Boy ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d01", "start": 413, "end": 496, "text": "[ 1 ] U2 singer Bono has said that he wrote the song from his mother 's perspective"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d02", "start": 0, "end": 35, "text": "The Old Grey Whistle Test in 1981 ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d02", "start": 36, "end": 126, "text": "The performance was later released on DVD on a compilation of performances from the show ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d02", "start": 127, "end": 277, "text": "[ 5 ] Reception and legacy [ edit ] [ ] In 2005 , Blender ranked the song at number 214 on its list `` The 500 Greatest Songs Since You Were Born '' ."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d02", "start": 278, "end": 396, "text": "The magazine wrote , `` The first song on U2 's first album introduced the guitar sound that would define their work ."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d02", "start": 397, "end": 402, "text": "[ ..."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d02", "start": 403, "end": 501, "text": "] The arena-ready clarion call also established Bono 's trademark lyrical earnestness , one of the"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d03", "start": 0, "end": 414, "text": "indicating in a four and a half star review at New Release Tuesday, realizes, \"The overarching theme of I Will Follow is to continue walking the path God has laid out for us, no matter how unexpected or uncomfortable...as much as the vocals and lyrics will be part of its success, the incredible instrumentation and background vocals stand out as a major part of why \"I Will Follow\" is such a well-rounded effort.\""}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d03", "start": 415, "end": 589, "text": "Specifying in a five star review from \"Worship Leader\", Steve Reed replies, \"\"I Will Follow\" is an amazing collection of musical expressions from the legendary Jeremy Camp..."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d04", "start": 0, "end": 286, "text": "I Will Follow (film) I Will Follow is a 2010 American independent drama film written, produced and directed by Ava DuVernay, starring Salli Richardson-Whitfield, Beverly Todd, Omari Hardwick, Michole White, Dijon Talton, Royale Watkins, Damone Roberts, Tracie Thoms and Blair Underwood."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d04", "start": 287, "end": 424, "text": "Maye (Salli Richardson-Whitfield) is a successful artist who has taken a leave from work to care for her ill aunt, Amanda (Beverly Todd)."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d04", "start": 425, "end": 593, "text": "As the film begins, Maye is moving out of the home she once shared with Amanda after her death and contemplating her relationships, her career, her past and her future."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d04", "start": 594, "end": 621, "text": "\"I Will Follow\" was shot in"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d05", "start": 0, "end": 124, "text": "Ebert gave the film three and a half out of four stars , describing it as `` a universal story about universal emotions '' ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d05", "start": 125, "end": 496, "text": "[ 6 ] Accolades [ edit ] African-American Film Critics Association [ 7 ] 2011 , Best Screenplay : Ava DuVernay ( Winner ) Black Reel Awards [ 8 ] 2012 , Best Screenplay : Ava DuVernay ( Nominated ) 2012 , Best Director : Ava DuVernay ( Nominated ) Image Awards [ 9 ] 2012 , Outstanding Independent Motion Picture ( Nominated ) See also [ edit ] List of black films of the"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0380-2ed353c21423:d06", "start": 0, "end": 613, "text": "of contents I Will Follow ( film ) Add languages Add links Article Talk English Read Edit View history